{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DERIVATION of the counts quoted in this ticket (recorded 2026-08-19 after validation flagged that\nthey do not reconcile with the calibration document's, and that neither was reproducible as stated).\n\nMethod used for THIS ticket's figures: scan every `.tickets-hotpath-authoritative/**/*-REVIEW_RESULT.json`;\nkeep events whose `data.schema` starts with `code_review_result`; segment by\n`data.impact_model_version == \"code-v3\"`; then count every string in `finding.criteria` across the\npools `blocking`, `advisory`, `dropped`, `indeterminate`, `coaching`. Result: 1663 sidecars, 5669\nlabel instances, of which 2338 (41.2%) are absent from the PACKAGED routing index —\nmaintainability 869, correctness 808, edge-cases 553, bugfix-size-attestation 61, clarity 14,\nproject.review-phase-boundaries 10, sec 8, documentation 5, concurrency 3, logic 2, consistency 2,\nrobustness 1, behavior-change 1, resource-management 1. (Across all versions a 15th appears,\n`observability`, from code-v2.)\n\nWHY THIS DIFFERS from the document's \"1760 sidecars / 1173 changes / 4359 pooled findings\" and its\n913/865/588/11: the document does not count raw labels. `calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py`'s\n`load()` buckets sidecars by `change_id` and segments into MATERIAL REVISION EPISODES (consecutive\nsidecars of the same change with different revisions), then pools findings per episode. That is a\ndeduplicating denominator; mine is a raw census. Neither is wrong — they measure different things —\nbut the two must never be compared directly, and this ticket should not be read as correcting the\ndocument's arithmetic.\n\nIMPLICATION for the Item 3 fix: whoever corrects the document must state which denominator each\nfigure uses. The uncorrected doc invites exactly the comparison error above, and the raw-vs-pooled\ndistinction is itself worth one sentence in the corrected text.\n\nThe ticket's ARGUMENT does not rest on these counts. It rests on: the base prompt's open \"e.g.\"\nvocabulary, the three-layer effective-criteria mechanism, and the absence of any normalization step\nbetween a finding's label and `threshold_for` — all confirmed independently against source."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787178654582232001,"uuid":"cebc6d91-246c-4a0e-8813-844b1c11154f"}